[REVIEWED 2026-11-15: SupermarketFixes/src/Patches/RackMoveFix.cs, v0.7.0, awaiting in-game test + host F8 log] Bug #1. When rearranging racks (not shelves), some of the boxes already in the rack will stay floating at the original location, instead of disappearing, and appearing with the rack on the new location. Those boxes end up being duplicated in some cases, since they will stay floating but also move with the rack. Some of the floating boxes can be picked up and moved, others just stay as ghost items, which the user can pass through but not interact with, and they remain until the game is reloaded. This mostly happens to the other computer (the guest, not the host) while playing online.
[REVIEWED 2026-11-15: SupermarketFixes/src/Patches/GhostHeldItemFix.cs, awaiting in-game test + logs] Bug #2: Sometimes the user is holding an item, then puts it down on the floor, but a ghost image of that item seems to remain in their hands. The user can freely interact with everything else, so the object doesn't count as being held, but it's still rendered in their hands until they reload the game. It doesn't interfere with gameplay, but it does block their view and look very strange and confusing
[REVIEWED 2026-11-15: SupermarketFixes/src/Patches/StuckBoxFix.cs, awaiting in-game test + logs] Bug #3: When buying boxes from the wholesale stores, sometimes the box stays right on top of the place where it was bought but it doesn't move from there. The user can now move around but they're not visually holding the box, however their controls are all intercepted by it. That means that the user does not appear to be holding anything, but left clicking just opens and closes the stationary box, and dropping or throwing it does nothing. They are now stuck to the box and need to reload the game since they can't interact with anything else. I noticed this happens especially with the ice cream cones on the general goods store.
Bug #4: The game randomly crashes for the other player (the guest, not the host) when playing multiplayer. i can't give more info than that because I haven't seen a specific reason why this happens. What can i do to record some logs or something that will help debug this issue.
[REVIEWED 2026-11-15: SupermarketFixes/src/Patches/BoxPlaceFix.cs, awaiting in-game test + logs] Bug #5: It happens often that you are not able to put items from the crate into a new shelf that doesn't have the label for this product yet. This is most noticeable when there was a different kind of product there before and the label was cleared. It should allow to put the new product in right away, but there is a good percentage of the times where it doesn't do that, and the user needs to unselect the crate, then open it again, and then the game lets you do it.
Bug #6: When there is a pile of boxes, like after placing a big online order, sometimes, taking the box from the bottom will not make the one on top of it drop, and it stays floating in the air until someone picks it up. I don't have more data to reproduce this bug but it happens relatively frequently. Might be related to bug #1.

