[REVIEWED 2026-11-15: PriceMarkupKeeper/, awaiting in-game test] Improvement #1: Make prices respect the global settings that are set through the pricing tab on the computer. I normally set it to 5% above market value, but on the next day, some prices will change, and they will not follow the previous rule. I want to make it so that, when the user set a global value for prices and discounts, they are still applied to those items whose prices went up or down at the beginning of the next day.
[DONE 2026-11-14] Improvement #2: Make paint cans last twice as long.
[IN PROGRESS: PlayerCrouch/, awaiting in-game test] Improvement #3: Add the ability of players to crouch, pressing Ctrl. Animate the characters to crouch when this happens.
[DONE 2026-11-14] Improvement #4: Make customers using self checkout machines 2x faster. Make the speed configurable as a float in the mod setings (i.e. 1.5x should be valid), up to 10x.
[IN PROGRESS: RestockerDoubleCarry/, awaiting in-game test] Improvement #5: Make level 10 restockers able to carry 2 boxes of products at a time. They will go to storage (or the outside dump where new boxes are delivered), pick up two boxes, then go restock the first product, then the second, then back to storage with what's left (if anything).
[IN PROGRESS: FurnitureMoveCancel/, awaiting in-game test] Improvement #6: When rearranging furniture (shelves/fridges/freezers/racks/etc), add an option to press escape and return them to where they were before being picked up, as long as the space is still free. If the item cannot be placed back where it was, then the key does nothing. Make sure to add it to the list of help keys on the side.
[IN PROGRESS: ExtraComputers/, written, awaiting in-game test] Improvement #7: Create a new furniture type that is the computer, for a price of $500. Players can buy as many of them as they want. When bought, they arrive in a box with a small icon outside, just as other furniture pieces. Players can then place them anywhere they want and they function the same as any other computers. Each of them has its own independent session (meaning, the screen of one is not mirrored to another), and can make any changes they want. If it would require a lot of work to keep those pages in sync when one of the players makes changes, then it is not necessary to live update the page for other users, if two players happen to be on the same page at the same time. Keep them independent for now and accept that one of them will have an outdated view if one player is making changes to it. However, if it is easy, or even simpler to keep them in sync and live update on the second computer, then that is obviously preferred.
Improvement #8: Make grid mode the default when placing furniture of any kind.
Improvement #9: Allow shift+right click to load all items from the shelf/fridge/freezer into the crate or paper bag, instead of having to hold it to put them in one by one. Works the other way too, so players can shift click to dump all items of the same type into the shelf at once. keep in mind that shelves and crates can hold more than one type of item but shelves cannot. when outputting into the shelf, only take the items that are of the same type as the shelf, following the same rules that the game currently does, and respecting the size limit of the shelf. both the crate and the bag have a size limit, so respect that too. use the standard animation for the products flying between the shelf and the container, but make it really fast so they move almost instantly, but following the standard animation so they don't just teleport in and out. make the key binding configurable in the mod settings. 
Improvement #10: Allow players to pick up two boxes at a time. In that case, the boxes cannot be opened, only carried and placed somewhere else. As soon as the player drops/throws/places one of the boxes, the other one can be opened and the products placed on shelves normally (the standard behavior of the game).
